From a7cf284b4fc0b271099fed2ebbbd31ed90d2e1d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:45:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 76/88] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x: fix the analog TX gain scale

The ADC1-ADC4 Volume controls (0-20) declared a 0.25 dB step and a mute
at 0. Measured on the OnePlus Pad 4 (1 kHz reference through both analog
mics, gains 0/6/12/14): +8.9, +8.9 and +3.0 dB, i.e. 1.5 dB per step, and
0 is not a mute (the reference is still captured). User space therefore
showed a 5 dB range where there are 30 dB, and treated the lowest gain as
muted.

Declare 1.5 dB per step without a mute.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
index aea27dc48..6d96b3932 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@ static const char * const wcd939x_supplies[] = {
 
 static const SNDRV_CTL_TLVD_DECLARE_DB_MINMAX(ear_pa_gain, 600, -1800);
 static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, 0, 7, 1);
-static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(analog_gain, 0, 25, 1);
+static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(analog_gain, 0, 150, 0);
 
 static const struct wcd_mbhc_field wcd_mbhc_fields[WCD_MBHC_REG_FUNC_MAX] = {
 	WCD_MBHC_FIELD(WCD_MBHC_L_DET_EN, WCD939X_ANA_MBHC_MECH, 0x80),
-- 
